ou build a PDF reader Android app!</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">I'll help you build a PDF reader Android app! Given your Python background and Jupyter notebook setup, the best approach is to use <strong>Kivy</strong> (Python framework for Android apps) or <strong>React Native/Flutter</strong>. But since you know Python, let's go with <strong>Buildozer + Kivy</strong> — pure Python to Android APK.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Here's your complete roadmap:</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">🗺️ Overview of Steps</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Install required tools on your laptop</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Write the PDF reader app in Python (Kivy)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Build it into an APK using Buildozer (on Linux/WSL)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Install APK on your Samsung Galaxy M12</li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — Set Up Your Environment</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Since you're on Windows (Intel i5), you need <strong>WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux)</strong> because Buildozer only works on Linux.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>In PowerShell (run as Administrator):</strong></p>
