<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">And press <strong>Enter</strong></p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">It may ask you to accept <strong>multiple licenses</strong> one by one — type <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">y</code> and Enter for each one. This is normal and required to use the Android SDK.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">After accepting all licenses, the build will continue automatically downloading and compiling everything.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">You're doing great — the build is progressing! 🎉</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
