df_reader:/home/user/hostcwd kivy/buildozer android debug</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">This uses an official Kivy Docker image that has everything pre-configured correctly — right NDK version, right clang, right cmake — all matching. No more version conflicts!</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Alternatively, if Docker feels complex, I'd suggest <strong>switching the entire approach to use a web-based builder called GitHub Actions</strong> — you push your code to GitHub and it builds the APK in the cloud and downloads it. Zero local build issues.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Which would you prefer?</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Option A</strong> — Try Docker (still local, but cleaner environment)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Option B</strong> — GitHub Actions (cloud build, easiest, always works)</li>
