 on your laptop first, then transfer to phone.</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Download it on your <strong>laptop</strong> first, then transfer to phone. Here's how:</p>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — Download on laptop</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Click <strong>"auto accept license"</strong> → scroll down → click <strong>"pdf-reader-apk"</strong> → it downloads as a <strong>zip file</strong> to your Downloads folder.</p>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 2 — Extract the zip</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Right-click the downloaded zip → <strong>Extract All</strong> → you'll find <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">pdfreader-0.1-debug.apk</code> inside.</p>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 3 — Transfer to phone</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Your Galaxy M12 was connected via USB earlier! Just:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Connect phone via USB cable</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">On phone — select <strong>"File Transfer"</strong> mode (not charging)</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Copy the APK file to your phone's <strong>Downloads</strong> folder</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 4 — Install on phone</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">On your Galaxy M12:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong>Settings → Apps → Special access → Install unknown apps</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Allow your file manager</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Open file manager → Downloads → tap the APK → <strong>Install</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Go click on the green "auto accept license" run and send a screenshot of the artifacts section! 📱</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
