ommon issue with Kivy apps!</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">This is a common issue with Kivy apps! The app crashes because it's missing some runtime libraries. Let's fix the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">main.py</code> to be more compatible with Android.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The most likely cause is the <strong>PIL/Pillow import</strong> — it doesn't work well on Android with Kivy. Let me give you a fixed version that uses only Kivy-native rendering.</p>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — Replace main.py completely</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Open <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">pdf-reader-app\main.py</code> in Notepad, delete everything, paste this simpler version:</p>
