<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Steps to add the icon:</h3>
<h4 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 1 — Save the icon</h4>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">You need to create an <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">icon.png</code> file. The easiest way:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Right-click the icon shown above → <strong>Save image as</strong> → save as <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">icon.png</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Put it in your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">pdf-reader-app</code> folder</li>
</ol>
<h4 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 2 — Update buildozer.spec</h4>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Change these lines:</p>
<div role="group" aria-label="ini code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
  items-center
  justify-center
